{
  "requirement": "The harness MUST construct each assessment's mandatory input set by combining\nthe contributions specified by the requirements applicable to that subject and\nits inputs. A requirement that contributes inputs MUST cite this requirement and\ndefine which sources it contributes and when. The harness MUST include every\napplicable contribution, deduplicate identical selections, and report\nunresolvable mandatory inputs before inference. The complete set MUST be supplied\nin the initial model request.\nA file selected as a mandatory input MUST be visible under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`. A denied selection MUST abort\nunder {cite}`requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "Add `{test}` to `src/authoring/inputs.rs#mod[tests]/fn[outside_test_anchors_stay_outside_the_project_with_an_allow_rule]` — The subject requires a mandatory-input file to be visible under `requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`, which excludes files outside the project directory. This test makes a `:test:` anchor point outside the project, by absolute path and by `../` path. It asserts that `AssessmentSources::prepare` aborts with PermissionDenied and an 'outside' message, and that an allow rule does not change that. It is the only test of the outside-project exclusion for mandatory inputs, but it is marked only for `requirements.references.anchors` and `requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`. It needs a `{test}` reference to `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs`.\n\nAdd `{test}` to `src/authoring/inputs.rs#mod[tests]/fn[mandatory_inputs_through_symlinks_leaving_the_project_abort_preparation]` — This test makes an `:impl:` anchor point at an in-project symlink whose target is outside the project. It asserts that preparation aborts with PermissionDenied and that the error names the path and says 'outside'. That checks the local_provider visibility rule and the abort for a mandatory input. It is not marked for `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs`.\n\nAdd a test, marked `{test}` for `requirements.authoring.mandatory_inputs`, in `src/authoring/inputs.rs` that covers the remaining local_provider exclusions. It should declare an anchor into Git metadata, such as `:test: .git/config`, and assert that `AssessmentSources::prepare` fails with PermissionDenied before inference. It should also cover a nested `.gitignore` with an exception, for example a negated pattern. The test should show that an excepted file is still supplied and that an ignored sibling is denied. — The subject requires mandatory-input files to be visible under `requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`. That requirement excludes Git metadata and honors nested ignore files and their exceptions. The reviewed tests only use a root `.gitignore` and a symlinked alias. The outside-project cases are covered by the two tests above, but not Git metadata or nested ignore files and exceptions. An implementation could therefore accept a `.git/` anchor, or ignore nested ignore rules and exceptions, and still pass the reviewed tests. The only `.git` tests I found are for reference discovery in `src/evidence.rs` and for the `read_node` tool in `tests/authoring_cli.rs`. Neither covers mandatory-input anchors.",
  "references": "528817a22486111257e77556ddd138b2ff22971a54040b26e8cb63bd67df9961",
